# Fine Print — environment variables
#
# Only the serverless coach function (api/coach.js) reads any of these.
# The browser code never sees them. Copy this file to .env.local for
# `vercel dev`, or set the same names as Environment Variables in the
# Vercel project (Settings → Environment Variables). Never commit .env.local.

# --- The one live model call -------------------------------------------------

# Gemini API key from Google AI Studio (free, no card). This is the only
# secret in the product. Without it the coach still answers, from the
# lesson's own written notes, and the reader sees no error.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Master switch for the live call. Leave unset or "0" during development so
# free-tier requests are not spent; set to "1" only for the smoke test, the
# post-deploy check, and the demo. Anything other than "1" means off.
USE_LIVE_AI=0

# Optional. Model name for generateContent. Defaults to gemini-3.1-flash-lite.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# --- Set by Vercel, not by you ----------------------------------------------

# VERCEL_ENV is "production" on the production deployment. When it is
# anything else the coach response carries a small `debug` field
# (reason, status, model) — never the key.
# VERCEL_ENV=development

# --- Local smoke test --------------------------------------------------------
# USE_LIVE_AI=1 GEMINI_API_KEY=... node scripts/coach_smoke.mjs
# Prints source and message; exits non-zero unless source === "live".
# See docs/COACH_SMOKE.md.
